@title 2026 Engagement Survey Results
@subtitle Northwind Freight, for all staff
@author HR team, Northwind Freight
@date 2026

Thank you to everyone who took part. Here is what you told us, how it compares with 2025, and what we will do next.

## Response

kpi Average favorable | 66.2% | +1.2 pts on 2025 | good

kpi Responses | 842 | of 1,060 employees
kpi Response rate | 79.4% | of all staff
kpi Lowest score | 49% | growth, down 3 pts | bad

## Results by statement

Share of respondents who answered favorably, neutrally or unfavorably, in percent.

data results = statement,favorable,neutral,unfavorable; I understand how my work supports company goals,78,15,7; My manager gives me useful feedback,64,22,14; I have the tools I need to do my job,71,18,11; I see a path to grow here,49,27,24; I would recommend this company as a place to work,69,20,11
chart hbar results stack unit=% max=100 title="How you answered each statement"

table results heat=favorable title="Results by statement (%)"

## Change since 2025

Favorable scores rose on four of five statements. Manager feedback and recommendation gained the most, 3 points each. The only decline was growth, down 3 points, which is also our lowest score.

data change = statement,favorable 2025,favorable 2026,change pts; I understand how my work supports company goals,76,78,2; My manager gives me useful feedback,61,64,3; I have the tools I need to do my job,70,71,1; I see a path to grow here,52,49,-3; I would recommend this company as a place to work,66,69,3
chart hbar change y=change pts unit=pts focus="I see a path to grow here" title="Change in favorable score since 2025"

table change title="Favorable score, 2025 and 2026 (%)"

## What we will do

We heard you most clearly on growth and feedback. These are our commitments:

1. Publish the career framework by 2027-02-28, so everyone can see how to grow here.
2. Train 90 managers on giving useful feedback, starting 2026-12-01.
3. Run a short pulse check in April 2027 to see whether things are moving.
